From 7b2f66ca7922b7c66e002682429f4152c80b6018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zehrer-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:14:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2835-sdhostd: move multi-block transfers with the BCM2835
 DMA controller

Channel 4 (if the devicetree mask leaves it free), one control block per
transfer paced by sdhost's DREQ 13, through a 64 KiB uncached bounce
buffer; polling for the end. Single blocks, the last 3 words of a
multi-block read (as Linux does) and the retry after a failed transfer
move through the FIFO with the CPU. SDHOSTD_NO_DMA turns DMA off.
